      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "tropica",
      "sourceUrl": "https://tropica.com/en/plants/plantdetails/Limnobiumlaevigatum(063TC)/4761",
      "html": "<ul><li>Origin: South America</li><li>Growth rate: medium</li><li>Height: 3 - 5+ cm (average after two months in the tank)</li><li>Light demand: low</li><li>CO2 demand: low</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "maintenance",
      "source": "tropica",
      "sourceUrl": "https://tropica.com/en/plants/plantdetails/Limnobiumlaevigatum(063TC)/4761",
      "html": "<p>If there are enough nutrients in the water and the light intensity is good, new leaves will appear above the water surface. It may become necessary to remove some so that the plants beneath still get some light. When the nutrient level in the water decreases, it will grow much slower, which makes it a great indicator of the available nutrients.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "tropica",
      "sourceUrl": "https://tropica.com/en/plants/plantdetails/Limnobiumlaevigatum(063TC)/4761",
      "html": "<p>Aquarium plant from tissue culture in closed cup. Limnobium laevigatum from South America is a decorative floating plant that is particularly suitable for open aquariums. It is 1-5 cm tall with leaves 5-15 cm wide. It is also good in traditional aquariums, because the fine, long and decorative roots provide protection to gouramies and other surface fish that like the roots of floating plants.</p>"
    }
  ],
